        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(feishu): use union_id as fallback for @mention detection in multi-bot groups",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nFixes #40768\n\nWhen multiple Feishu bots share the same group, @mentioning a specific bot is not recognized. The bot logs `message in group ... did not mention bot` even though it's correctly mentioned.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nFeishu `open_id` is **app-scoped** — the same bot has a different `open_id` depending on which app's token is used to query it. Confirmed by querying the same message with two different bot tokens:\n\n```\n# Same @mention, different app contexts:\nwriter token → mention open_id: ou_4ede388c79638a9057a432c3e3832f91\ntron token   → mention open_id: ou_04dc13327d491d9e36da57826a4131f0\n```\n\nWebSocket push events deliver mention `open_id`s in a specific app context that may not match the receiving bot's own `open_id`, causing `checkBotMentioned()` to always return `false`.\n\n## Fix\n\n`union_id` is globally unique across all apps for the same entity — it doesn't vary by app context. This PR:\n\n1. Fetches `union_id` alongside `open_id` from `bot/v3/info` at startup\n2. Stores it in a new `botUnionIds` map in monitor state\n3. Passes it through to `checkBotMentioned()` as a fallback\n4. Matches mentions by `union_id` when `open_id` doesn't match\n\nThe `open_id` match is preserved as the primary check; `union_id` is a fallback, so existing behavior is unchanged for single-bot setups.\n\n## Files Changed\n\n- `types.ts`: add `botUnionId` to `FeishuProbeResult`\n- `probe.ts`: extract `union_id` from `bot/v3/info` response\n- `monitor.startup.ts`: propagate `botUnionId` through `FeishuMonitorBotIdentity`\n- `monitor.state.ts`: add `botUnionIds` map with proper clear/delete\n- `monitor.account.ts`: store/clear `botUnionId`, pass to `handleFeishuMessage`\n- `bot.ts`: accept `botUnionId` in `checkBotMentioned` and `parseFeishuMessageEvent`, match by `union_id` when `open_id` mismatches",
        "branch": "fix/feishu-mention-union-id",
